WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:05.520
everyone knows that 0 *&nbsp;
anything equals 0, but why?

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:09.720
your intuition is probably telling you&nbsp;
that multiplication is repeated addition

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:14.440
and if I add zero copies of something&nbsp;
then of course I have zero things

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:17.920
if you have a bit of math knowledge&nbsp;
you might go beyond intuition and say

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:23.280
"that's just how multiplication is defined:&nbsp;
0 is the base case, 0 * anything equals 0,

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:30.160
and multiplication of larger numbers is&nbsp;
defined by saying (y + 1) * x = y * x + x"

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.640
but we use the symbol "0" for a lot&nbsp;
more than just the natural numbers

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.560
0 the natural number * anything equals 0

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:40.840
0 the real number times anything equals 0

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:44.520
0 in modular arithmetic times anything equals 0

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:47.560
the 0 matrix * anything equals 0

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:51.040
the constant zero function times anything equals 0

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:55.280
and even the zero function&nbsp;
convolution anything equals zero

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.520
these are all different types of zeros&nbsp;
and different types of multiplication

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.280
they're definitely not simple repeated addition

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:06.720
and yet we still end up with&nbsp;
0 * anything equals 0, why?

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:11.040
let's prove it and see what about&nbsp;
zero actually makes this happen

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:13.840
start with the expression 0 * x

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.880
for now you can assume these are real numbers

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:19.200
but we'll see shortly that's not necessary

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:24.240
0 is 0+ 0 because 0 plus anything is that thing

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:29.600
then because addition distributes&nbsp;
this is 0 * x plus 0 * x

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:34.440
at this point in the proof we don't know that 0&nbsp;
* x equals 0 but we know that it's some number

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.120
and we know that number has a negative

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:41.520
so let's add that negative&nbsp;
to both sides of the equation

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:43.720
then group with parens

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:49.240
and since a number plus its negative&nbsp;
is zero we get 0 = 0 + 0 * x

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:51.880
and since again 0 plus anything is that thing

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:56.080
we finally arrive at 0 * x = 0

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:01.360
in this proof the only facts we really used&nbsp;
are: that 0 plus anything equals that thing,

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:04.240
that addition distributes over multiplication,

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:07.320
that every number has a negative&nbsp;
that cancels it to give zero,

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:11.280
and if you want to be real technical we&nbsp;
did also use associativity to group parens

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:14.600
we don't even need commutativity&nbsp;
of addition or multiplication

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:18.440
which is good because matrix&nbsp;
multiplication is not commutative

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:21.360
if you're applying for grad&nbsp;
school you might describe this as

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:25.800
"the identity for an associative&nbsp;
invertible operation is absorbing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:29.760
for any other operation that&nbsp;
distributes over the first"

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:34.920
that's why it works for matrices,&nbsp;
functions, convolutions, and many more

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:38.320
because all these types of&nbsp;
objects satisfy common axioms

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:41.840
which in particular include the properties we need

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:45.520
and no this does not prove&nbsp;
that 0 * Infinity equals 0

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:49.960
the proof only works if 0 * Infinity is&nbsp;
defined so that we can do algebra on it

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:54.360
but 0 * Infinity isn't defined so no proof

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:56.360
although if you're a teacher it's a fun exercise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:59.760
to ask your students to explain why&nbsp;
the proof breaks down for Infinity

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:04.280
anyway you're probably wondering&nbsp;
"well what about those assumptions?"

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:07.960
is there a similar trick to show that&nbsp;
0 plus anything equals that thing?

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:10.520
it feels like a very similar kind of problem

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:13.520
usually this is just shown manually&nbsp;
because the behavior of zero under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:17.240
addition is closely aligned to&nbsp;
the definition of addition itself

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:20.600
a lot of the time you give the label&nbsp;
zero to an element of your number system

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:24.880
precisely because it has the property&nbsp;
that it does nothing under your addition

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:29.040
so maybe the real question is "how do&nbsp;
we normally define addition at all?"

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:32.120
great question, maybe a topic for another video

